  "summary": "Five preprints released 24–25 November describe open platforms and agents for single-cell, cryo-EM and molecular dynamics analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is software that lowers the barrier to analyzing complex biological data, spanning single-cell omics, cryo-EM and molecular simulation. SingloCell offers browser-based exploration of multimodal single-cell data, and CyteArc analyzes remote atlases in place at roughly 100-million-cell scale with provenance tracking. EM-Claw and Molpylot use language-model agents: EM-Claw guides cryo-EM single-particle analysis from accumulated experience, and Molpylot exposes 256 typed tools in a shared human-AI workspace for biomolecular simulation. VMDance brings n-ary similarity clustering and representative selection into VMD as an interactive plugin. The items differ in domain; the dominant emphasis is on implementation: interactivity, reuse, provenance and agent-operable workflows rather than new biological findings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
